{
  "format_version": 1,
  "spec": "specs.md §21.2",
  "description": "What a path of Atoll's own view resolves to once the view's own operations that no pass has taken in are laid over the catalog, newest first, and what a folder's listing may hold. A path made, written, renamed or hard-linked to presents what its disk holds there, read at the path itself (kind disk); a path deleted, removed, replaced or renamed from, and anything below a folder removed or renamed from, presents nothing (kind absent); any other presents the catalog's rows at the first of paths that presents something: below a folder renamed, the path below its old name, then each later name, the path itself last (kind catalog). A folder's listing holds the names the catalog lists at each of catalog_dirs, and names, those the operations made or renamed directly below it, carried through the folders renamed since, in byte order; each name is then resolved on its own, and one that presents nothing is left out. An operation has kind create, mkdir, symlink, write, rename, replace, link, unlink or rmdir, the disk it was made on, its path, and path2 for a rename, a replacement or a hard link, whose path is the name it was made from and path2 the new name, which presents what its disk holds there while the name it was made from stays as it was; folder says that it names a folder.",
  "cases": [
    {"ops": [], "path": "F/a.mkv", "source": {"kind": "catalog", "paths": ["F/a.mkv"]}, "note": "no operation: the catalog's rows for the path"},
    {"ops": [{"kind": "create", "disk": "t2", "path": "F/new.mkv"}], "path": "F/new.mkv", "source": {"kind": "disk", "disk": "t2"}, "note": "a file made presents what its disk holds there"},
    {"ops": [{"kind": "create", "disk": "t2", "path": "F/new.mkv"}], "path": "F/a.mkv", "source": {"kind": "catalog", "paths": ["F/a.mkv"]}, "note": "an operation elsewhere changes nothing"},
